  "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{14}$ are I.I.D random variables, where\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(5,{2}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 14,\n$$\n\ncalculate $P(70\\le Y\\le 78),$ where  $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{14}.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ | $\\,0.8770\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ | $\\,0.8962\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ |",
